        'For a simple quantizer with step Δ, rounding to the nearest grid point gives an error e with |e| ≤ Δ/2 when no clipping occurs. If the scale makes Δ too large, representability error grows; if the range is too narrow, clipping adds a larger, biased error. The useful question is therefore an error budget tied to the tensor and operation, not “how many bits?” alone.',
